WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.020
- This is what your hair
looks like when it's dirty.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.630
- [Narrator] And this is what
shampoo does to that dirt.

00:00:06.630 --> 00:00:10.110
- Surfactants form these
micelles around the dirt,

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.780
which is what grabs onto dirt and oil.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.380
It's like, no, no, I don't wanna go.

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:17.786
That was the dirt.

00:00:17.786 --> 00:00:20.910
It's screaming for its life. (laughs)

00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:22.980
- [Narrator] Erica Douglas
has been a cosmetic chemist

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:24.120
for more than a decade,

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.370
and today she's going to
break down the ingredients

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.100
in Head &amp; Shoulders Classic
Clean dandruff shampoo.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.250
- It's about to get messy. (laughs)

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.920
It's actually a fairly simple formula.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.240
Not a lot of ingredients.

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:39.060
That means that there's not a
lot of fluff in this formula.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:40.440
- [Narrator] Erica broke
down the ingredients

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.674
into these categories.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.020
Let's start here.

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:44.700
- One of the first ingredients that I see

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.070
is pyrithione zinc.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.050
This is one of the most common actives

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:52.230
used in the cosmetic
space to fight dandruff.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:55.020
Without this ingredient,
it's just the shampoo.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.750
Dandruff is actually caused by a fungus

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.600
called Malassezia, and
it feeds on the oil.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.210
- [Narrator] The FDA allows
up to 2% of pyrithione zinc

00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:04.650
in products like this shampoo,

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.480
which are applied and then rinsed off.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.840
The Classic Clean formula
uses pyrithione zinc at 1%.

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:10.800
But in the EU.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:13.290
- They actually banned pyrithione zinc

00:01:16.793 --> 00:01:19.133
mutagenic, or toxic for reproduction.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:20.123
According to the company,

00:01:20.123 --> 00:01:22.073
the EU version uses this ingredient

00:01:22.073 --> 00:01:23.783
instead of pyrithione zinc.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:26.153
So the active ingredient
handles the dandruff,

00:01:26.153 --> 00:01:27.923
but surfactants like these sulfates

00:01:27.923 --> 00:01:29.753
are what actually clean the scalp.

00:01:29.753 --> 00:01:33.593
- Surfactants are the
soapy part of the shampoo.

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:35.213
It's what causes the suds,

00:01:35.213 --> 00:01:37.313
it's actually what is pulling

00:01:37.313 --> 00:01:40.313
the dirt and the oil off
of your hair and scalp.

00:01:40.313 --> 00:01:42.353
I believe that they are using this

00:01:42.353 --> 00:01:46.313
as their primary surfactant,
and the cocamidopropyl betaine

00:01:46.313 --> 00:01:49.025
is the secondary
surfactant in this formula.

00:01:49.025 --> 00:01:51.593
- [Narrator] Surfactants work
a little something like this.

00:01:51.593 --> 00:01:53.933
- We're gonna just use
some regular pepper,

00:01:53.933 --> 00:01:57.983
have it float on top of
some normal deionized water.

00:01:57.983 --> 00:02:01.343
These surfactants have
their hydrophilic head

00:02:01.343 --> 00:02:06.083
and their hydrophobic tails,
and so they form these micelles

00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:10.313
around the dirt, which is
what grabs onto dirt and oil,

00:02:10.313 --> 00:02:13.193
and helps it to remove it

00:02:13.193 --> 00:02:14.633
from the hair and the scalp.

00:02:14.633 --> 00:02:16.793
Instantly you see how it repels it.

00:02:16.793 --> 00:02:19.463
It's like running from the shampoo.

00:02:19.463 --> 00:02:20.603
- [Narrator] Some surfactants create

00:02:20.603 --> 00:02:22.253
more suds than others, but.

00:02:22.253 --> 00:02:24.083
- Foam actually doesn't dictate

00:02:24.083 --> 00:02:26.483
how well a shampoo is cleaning your hair.

00:02:26.483 --> 00:02:28.373
There are certain surfactants

00:02:28.373 --> 00:02:31.793
that can produce a lot
of foam like this one,

00:02:31.793 --> 00:02:35.243
but then there are other
surfactants that are more mild.

00:02:35.243 --> 00:02:37.193
Does not mean that it's not working.

00:02:37.193 --> 00:02:39.656
So foam is kind of like for aesthetics.

00:02:39.656 --> 00:02:42.443
And we call this the
cylinder shake method.

00:02:42.443 --> 00:02:45.743
You can see how much
foam is going to last,

00:02:45.743 --> 00:02:47.963
and how it separates out.

00:02:47.963 --> 00:02:52.963
A lot of hairstylists view
sulfates as being too harsh.

00:02:53.153 --> 00:02:56.603
I see sulfates as a great surfactant

00:02:56.603 --> 00:03:01.013
when used in moderation, and
they're also being formulated

00:03:01.013 --> 00:03:03.782
in conjunction with
other conditioning agents

00:03:03.782 --> 00:03:08.033
that allow it to moisturize
and condition the hair

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:09.083
at the same time.

00:03:09.083 --> 00:03:11.123
- [Narrator] That's the job
of this ingredient here,

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:12.743
otherwise known as a silicone.

00:03:12.743 --> 00:03:16.283
- They help to maintain the
water level in your hair.

00:03:16.283 --> 00:03:21.283
This is water with just a
little bit of Violet 1 colorant,

00:03:21.323 --> 00:03:25.133
versus when I do the same
thing with dimethicone.

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:26.873
And dimethicone just has a little bit

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:29.003
of the Blue 1 colorant.

00:03:29.003 --> 00:03:32.273
You notice how the water went
right through the sponge.

00:03:32.273 --> 00:03:33.623
That's because it soaked in

00:03:33.623 --> 00:03:35.033
and went straight to the bottom,

00:03:35.033 --> 00:03:38.303
versus this silicone stain right on top.

00:03:38.303 --> 00:03:39.383
This is the difference between

00:03:39.383 --> 00:03:41.933
when your hair is absorbing moisture,

00:03:41.933 --> 00:03:45.323
versus using a silicone like dimethicone

00:03:45.323 --> 00:03:48.923
to help seal the cuticle and
maintain moisture content.

00:03:48.923 --> 00:03:51.923
Silicones have really gotten this bad rep.

00:03:51.923 --> 00:03:54.803
They've been thought
to weigh the hair down

00:03:54.803 --> 00:03:57.113
or leave a buildup.

00:03:57.113 --> 00:03:59.333
This is absolutely not true.

00:03:59.333 --> 00:04:03.263
They have the ability to stay on the hair,

00:04:03.263 --> 00:04:06.593
to seal the cuticles, and
they do come off the hair

00:04:06.593 --> 00:04:09.503
when using a shampoo.

00:04:09.503 --> 00:04:11.213
- [Narrator] Now, for
what gives the shampoo

00:04:11.213 --> 00:04:12.473
it's distinct look.

00:04:12.473 --> 00:04:17.473
- So Head &amp; Shoulders
uses Blue 1 and Red 33

00:04:17.663 --> 00:04:19.823
as their colorants, and that's how you get

00:04:19.823 --> 00:04:23.903
this really cool light blue looking color.

00:04:23.903 --> 00:04:26.843
In addition to the glycol distearate,

00:04:26.843 --> 00:04:28.973
which is used as a pearlizing agent

00:04:28.973 --> 00:04:30.833
to give it that pearl look.

00:04:30.833 --> 00:04:33.028
I don't know what the
ratios are that they use.

00:04:33.028 --> 00:04:35.603
That's their proprietary information.

00:04:35.603 --> 00:04:39.618
First, I'm gonna start
with my blue number one.

00:04:39.618 --> 00:04:44.603
Ooh, okay, and then we'll
try to see what happens

00:04:44.603 --> 00:04:47.783
when we add a little Red 33.

00:04:47.783 --> 00:04:51.293
As you can see, I literally
put less than a gram in,

00:04:51.293 --> 00:04:52.763
and that's how dark it got.

00:04:52.763 --> 00:04:55.493
- [Narrator] Blue 1 and Red
33 are both synthetic colors

00:04:55.493 --> 00:04:58.643
approved for use in cosmetics
with some use restrictions.

00:04:58.643 --> 00:05:01.313
- Some of the concerns that
come around synthetic colors

00:05:01.313 --> 00:05:03.413
would be that it could
potentially be an irritant

00:05:03.413 --> 00:05:05.363
or an allergen for some people.

00:05:05.363 --> 00:05:07.073
- [Narrator] According to the
environmental working group,

00:05:07.073 --> 00:05:09.893
Safety Ratings, Blue 1
is marked as high hazard

00:05:09.893 --> 00:05:12.053
while Red 33 is marked as moderate.

00:05:12.053 --> 00:05:14.063
A Head &amp; Shoulders
representative reiterated

00:05:14.063 --> 00:05:16.043
that these dyes are FDA approved,

00:05:16.043 --> 00:05:17.753
noting that the Classic Clean formula

00:05:17.753 --> 00:05:19.651
is known for its signature blue color.

00:05:19.651 --> 00:05:21.653
And when it comes to fragrance.

00:05:21.653 --> 00:05:23.873
- It just lists that they use fragrance.

00:05:23.873 --> 00:05:25.133
Nothing else.

00:05:25.133 --> 00:05:29.243
Fragrance contains 30,
40 ingredients sometimes.

00:05:29.243 --> 00:05:31.193
The ingredients that make up a fragrance

00:05:31.193 --> 00:05:32.783
are often proprietary.

00:05:32.783 --> 00:05:35.183
- [Narrator] But according to
Erica's scientific sniffer.

00:05:35.183 --> 00:05:37.383
- Product has floral

00:05:39.683 --> 00:05:41.543
and aquatic notes.

00:05:41.543 --> 00:05:43.073
- [Narrator] While it's
not listed on the label,

00:05:43.073 --> 00:05:45.503
Head &amp; Shoulders does
list over 20 ingredients

00:05:45.503 --> 00:05:48.473
found in the Classic Clean
fragrance formulation online,

00:05:48.473 --> 00:05:50.963
including some considered
allergens in the EU.

00:05:50.963 --> 00:05:53.753
And soon, this could become
a more common practice.

00:05:53.753 --> 00:05:56.363
- A new law was put into action

00:05:56.363 --> 00:05:59.993
which actually will now
require cosmetic products

00:05:59.993 --> 00:06:04.403
to list fragrance allergens
on the label going into 2024.

00:06:04.403 --> 00:06:06.413
- [Narrator] Consistency
is also a crucial part

00:06:06.413 --> 00:06:07.913
of a shampoo's formulation.

00:06:07.913 --> 00:06:09.593
- Some of the ingredients
that they're using

00:06:09.593 --> 00:06:14.453
to give that thick, creamy
feel is glycol distearate,

00:06:14.453 --> 00:06:19.193
also the guar hydroxypropyl
trimonium chloride.

00:06:19.193 --> 00:06:22.373
Guar is a great conditioning
detangling agent,

00:06:22.373 --> 00:06:24.923
but it also gives the
formula some thickness.

00:06:24.923 --> 00:06:28.343
With salt can give you that thick feel.

00:06:28.343 --> 00:06:30.233
- [Narrator] And while the
final product feels thick.

00:06:30.233 --> 00:06:33.113
- The most surprising thing
about shampoo formulations

00:06:33.113 --> 00:06:34.780
is that it's mostly water.

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:38.123
Any product that has water
in it has the potential

00:06:38.123 --> 00:06:41.829
to grow mold, fungus, bacteria.

00:06:41.829 --> 00:06:44.393
Ugh, we don't want any of that stuff.

00:06:44.393 --> 00:06:45.226
- [Narrator] Different packages

00:06:45.226 --> 00:06:46.373
The Wall Street Journal purchased

00:06:46.373 --> 00:06:47.813
had different preservatives listed.

00:06:47.813 --> 00:06:51.353
- The preservative used in this
product is sodium benzoate.

00:06:51.353 --> 00:06:52.913
- [Narrator] Another
version of the same product

00:06:52.913 --> 00:06:54.953
lists these two additional preservatives,

00:06:54.953 --> 00:06:56.972
which have a high incidence
with skin allergies.

00:06:56.972 --> 00:06:59.093
The company said it recently shifted away

00:06:59.093 --> 00:07:00.713
from this preservative combination

00:07:00.713 --> 00:07:02.273
to one with sodium benzoate.

00:07:02.273 --> 00:07:03.713
But products with the combination

00:07:03.713 --> 00:07:06.383
are still currently sold on store shelves.

00:07:06.383 --> 00:07:07.668
Before a product hits the shelf,

00:07:07.668 --> 00:07:10.373
one crucial element must be tested.

00:07:10.373 --> 00:07:11.723
That's the pH.

00:07:11.723 --> 00:07:14.843
- We are measuring a pH of 7.3

00:07:14.843 --> 00:07:16.943
for this Head &amp; Shoulders product.

00:07:16.943 --> 00:07:19.793
This is not abnormal,
but it is on the high end

00:07:19.793 --> 00:07:21.263
of what I would normally see.

00:07:21.263 --> 00:07:23.093
- [Narrator] Head &amp; Shoulders
said this reading is in line

00:07:23.093 --> 00:07:24.983
with the standard range of its formulas,

00:07:24.983 --> 00:07:26.453
which it said remains America's

00:07:26.453 --> 00:07:28.283
number one anti-dandruff shampoo

00:07:28.283 --> 00:07:29.933
with moisture levels as they are.

00:07:29.933 --> 00:07:32.753
And there are few things to
note on the overall packaging.

00:07:32.753 --> 00:07:36.653
- They claim that this
bottle is paraben free.

00:07:36.653 --> 00:07:40.253
I would agree that this
is a paraben free product.

00:07:40.253 --> 00:07:44.453
The paraben issue is a
very provocative topic.

00:07:44.453 --> 00:07:47.363
There have been some
preliminary studies that show

00:07:47.363 --> 00:07:49.373
that there could be possible linkage

00:07:49.373 --> 00:07:51.923
between parabens and cancer.

00:07:51.923 --> 00:07:54.799
There's no conclusive scientific data

00:07:54.799 --> 00:07:59.683
that links paraben usage and
cosmetics directly to cancer,

00:07:59.683 --> 00:08:03.593
but the possibilities
of it being a carcinogen

00:08:03.593 --> 00:08:08.423
has provoked some limitations
on how this ingredient

00:08:08.423 --> 00:08:10.673
is being used in the cosmetic space.

00:08:10.673 --> 00:08:11.506
- [Narrator] And Erica sees

00:08:11.506 --> 00:08:12.991
some opportunities for improvements.

00:08:12.991 --> 00:08:15.233
- If I could change
anything about this formula,

00:08:15.233 --> 00:08:16.886
I would probably add a few more

00:08:16.886 --> 00:08:19.613
conditioning and moisturizing agents

00:08:19.613 --> 00:08:21.743
just to give more functionality

00:08:21.743 --> 00:08:23.663
and more control to the actual hair.

00:08:23.663 --> 00:08:26.033
I think that dandruff
is a little hush hush

00:08:26.033 --> 00:08:29.873
because nobody wants to
be known as the snowflake.

00:08:29.873 --> 00:08:31.733
I think a lot of people associate dandruff

00:08:31.733 --> 00:08:34.883
with being unclean, but
that's completely not true.

00:08:34.883 --> 00:08:37.277
We need to talk more about it.

00:08:37.277 --> 00:08:40.444
(upbeat bright music)

